#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fadf4f64-3569-56b2-98e1-f6681892054a" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Orthogonality of Sines and Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "851f09d0-7ced-5315-ace2-af4ba03827ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164839} {:answer/id #uuid "7a4f664e-2478-5586-814e-35ea30c3fcc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a4f664e-2478-5586-814e-35ea30c3fcc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164840} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3d4c340-9073-5cc1-b1b3-42eb58ad14a1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164838} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8d4b0e1-03cf-5d7d-a5b3-5f5bd61544a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "− 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164842} {:answer/id #uuid "cd59fb54-c94e-5f86-8331-e045010a4a19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164843} {:answer/id #uuid "fd182b97-e8a4-5798-a3a9-833e5a890724" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164844} {:answer/id #uuid "2b1420ca-7a02-59c0-81cc-68fadbc8b0dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164845} {:answer/id #uuid "61b9c39e-a590-5f4f-9d71-37c7cecf4fb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61b9c39e-a590-5f4f-9d71-37c7cecf4fb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164846} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f9ce23b-0ab3-55e7-ba4d-ae8d90d6e1e1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "beb5a495-580f-541a-b622-3503782168cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-340367" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We begin by using the half-angle identity\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)=\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-6\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ $\\text{are not orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fadf4f64-3569-56b2-98e1-f6681892054a" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Orthogonality of Sines and Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90635441-91e9-5231-82e8-1f7783c24364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344907} {:answer/id #uuid "7b385cee-f562-51ce-8889-0cac72fa1968" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344908} {:answer/id #uuid "d707a58f-d523-53a4-bf56-17c7a61b3c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344909} {:answer/id #uuid "82c3a7ac-58b4-55ba-a0c9-59222e0a368c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d707a58f-d523-53a4-bf56-17c7a61b3c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344909} :answer-field/id #uuid "e719573d-a1ae-52d7-8449-6d6cb14f7307" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344906} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38b55a66-370d-58db-aa01-d558179ae875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344912} {:answer/id #uuid "78a17764-272d-51ea-a2c4-425663346554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38b55a66-370d-58db-aa01-d558179ae875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344912} :answer-field/id #uuid "075010aa-4b9b-5ca1-934f-b98275e5e7d3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1459f84b-ac32-5a32-9ee7-e5678c3f1aac" :question/math-academy-id "q-340368" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{18}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3\\pi ))+\\frac{1}{18}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-9\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-0)+\\frac{1}{18}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Expressions For Fourier Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4c691d6-4bec-5f7d-9461-b11507362ac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344916} {:answer/id #uuid "556a2fc0-5ef3-55ec-a341-2adecb3d35d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344917} {:answer/id #uuid "28fe17d1-4285-5906-bde9-838a72acbf5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344918} {:answer/id #uuid "a18dc9b6-1